{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1302241-pattern-spider-youtube-channel","id":1302241,"title":"Pattern Spider Youtube Channel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-03T09:18:40-07:00","id":1302241,"title":"Pattern Spider Youtube Channel","content":"Last year, I set up a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCoXdLZjZdKeC0ddHXBHHlQw\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Youtube channel</b></a> partially to practice my English and partially because I felt that a Youtube full of DnD has been lacking in Exalted content. The original idea was to create a resource for Exalted material. I decided never to advertise it because I became a freelancer for OPP and was uncertain what it would be okay for me to create and share. I made some other videos instead, but eventually checked in with the devs and got approval to keep making Exalted-related videos as long as I don't spoil any secret information and things like that. So to celebrate this, I made one video recently where I compared the stunting rules in all three editions, and then made a chargen guide for creating a DB in 3E. There's already quite a lot of videos on the site, including one video about Machineborn; an original game I'm writing.<br /> <br /> I decided to advertise the channel now because of this, and I'm going to make more Exalted-related non-spoiling content. I also welcome suggestions for topics you'd like to see adressed in future videos. It doesn't have to be Exalted stuff, and it doesn't have to be 3E only. I currently have the following video categories: <i>General RPG Discussions</i>, <i>RPG System Discussions</i>, <i>RPG Product Discussions &amp; Reviews</i> (these will be mostly about other games), <i>RPG Player Tips</i>, <i>RPG Storyteller Tips</i>, <i>RPG Design</i>, and <i>Roleplaying Journals</i>. You may request for any of them (or for more). Some of the upcoming stuff that I'm planning to do are journals talking about all games I've ran for 3E (one such video is already up), a thorough analysis of the V5 corebook, as well as a general discussion video about roleplaying online. If you want me to look at specific game systems that aren't Exalted, I'd be happy to take such requests as well. The only thing I'm not going to do is DnD-related videos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T15:08:37-07:00","id":1302352,"title":"","content":"I found this channel a while back. Good stuff reminded me why I love exalted lore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T12:46:37-07:00","id":1304292,"title":"","content":"I follow Pattern Spider on Youtube!!<br /> I like all your videos, they are really helpfull =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you like Alchemicals, please check out my DeviantArt Gallery!! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" bo